IMPORT prelude

-- Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019 (NSW) -- the dates and business days, in one small module. It uses only the
-- built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH), not the daydate
-- library, and defines no YMD.
--
-- cl 11(1) "business day means a day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday throughout New South Wales."
-- cl 11(2) "Unless the parties otherwise agree, the period from the beginning of 25 December until the end of 9 January
-- next following is to be ignored for the purpose of reckoning the time fixed by this Regulation for the doing by a party
-- of any act in connection with the claims resolution process."
--
-- Public holidays throughout NSW are fixed by another Act (a borrowed term), so they are not computed here: a question
-- that counts business days takes, as a fact, how many of them fall on a weekday in the period (see NOTES.md, fork F3).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2022). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Dust Diseases Tribunal Regulation 2019`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the regulation date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus calendar days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar days from` `the first day` `until` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

-- DATE_SERIAL modulo 7 is 0 on a Sunday and 6 on a Saturday (checked: 8 November 2026, a Sunday, gives 0).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls on a weekend` `the day` MEANS
        (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 0
    OR  (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 6

-- cl 11(2): from the beginning of 25 December until the end of 9 January next following.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`falls in the Christmas period` `the day` MEANS
        (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 25)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST 9)

-- A day counted when reckoning a time under Part 3: a weekday, and (unless the parties agreed otherwise) not in the
-- Christmas period. Weekday public holidays are added by the caller as extra days.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the Christmas period is ignored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is counted as a business day` `the day` `the Christmas period is ignored` MEANS
        (NOT (`falls on a weekend` `the day`))
    AND (NOT (`the Christmas period is ignored` AND `falls in the Christmas period` `the day`))

-- The day on which a period of n business days after `the day` ends: count forward from the next day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE, `the Christmas period is ignored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of` n `business days after` `the day` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `is counted as a business day` `the next day` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         THEN `the end of` (n MINUS 1) `business days after` `the next day` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         ELSE `the end of` n `business days after` `the next day` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the day` `plus calendar days` 1

-- The latest day that is at least n business days before `the event day`: count backward from the day before.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the event day` IS A DATE, `the Christmas period is ignored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day` n `business days before` `the event day` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored` MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN `the event day`
    ELSE IF `is counted as a business day` `the day before` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         THEN `the latest day` (n MINUS 1) `business days before` `the day before` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         ELSE `the latest day` n `business days before` `the day before` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
    WHERE
        `the day before` MEANS `the event day` `plus calendar days` (0 MINUS 1)

-- How many counted business days fall after `the first day` up to and including `the second day` (0 if the second is
-- not later). Used to put a dated act on a regulative rule's business-day clock.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE, `the Christmas period is ignored` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the business days after` `the first day` `up to` `the second day` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the second day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the first day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `is counted as a business day` `the second day` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         THEN 1 PLUS `the business days after` `the first day` `up to` `the day before` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
         ELSE `the business days after` `the first day` `up to` `the day before` `ignoring Christmas` `the Christmas period is ignored`
    WHERE
        `the day before` MEANS `the second day` `plus calendar days` (0 MINUS 1)

-- Schedule 1, Part 2, cl 3: "rounded to the nearest dollar and an amount of 50 cents is to be rounded down".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest dollar, 50 cents down` x MEANS CEILING (x MINUS 0.5)

